### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Order API — CHECKOUT (POST /api/v1/orders)
#
# How to run: VS Code REST Client — click "Send Request" top to bottom.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Docker stack up with the Order module: docker compose up -d --build
#   - Seeded chain admin exists: admin@devtunde.com / Password123!
#
# Contract (ticket 0016):
#   - CASHIER/MANAGER with an ACTIVE session only (title gate + session
#     gate; session-shaped 409s fire BEFORE basket validation).
#   - Snapshot (Q3): name + price frozen at sale; ALL money in kobo.
#   - Counter-settled v1 (Q4): CASH/CARD/TRANSFER, optional reference.
#   - Shortfall (Q6): 409 with per-line availability, NOTHING committed.
#   - Customer (Q5/Q8): optional phone, normalized at the boundary,
#     unknown phone = 400 (never silently unattached).
#
# `# Expected:` labels the status each request proves.
# Tokens expire after 15 MINUTES — re-send the setup from the top.
# Captures are session-scoped: a "No value is resolved" error means
# re-send the setup requests from the top of this file.
# All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1 — Setup: chain admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: mint the store's seat admin (fresh persona per run)
# @name seatSignup
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Order Seat Admin",
  "email": "ord-seat-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567"
}

### 3 — Setup: seat admin logs in
# @name seatLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{seatSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Setup: chain admin creates the store, seating that admin
# @name store
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brand": "Order Probe Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{seatLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Probe Way",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "ord-store-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — Setup: seat admin hires a cashier (the password we send IS the password)
# @name hire
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Order Cashier",
  "email": "ord-cashier-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234568",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 6 — Setup: the hired cashier logs in
# @name cashierLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hire.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 7 — Setup: the cashier opens a session (every checkout rides on it)
# @name session
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8 — Setup: chain admin creates a category
# @name category
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Order Probe Category {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 9 — Setup: the seat admin lists a product (₦12,000.00 selling price)
# @name listing
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/store/{{store.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Probe Milk 1L",
  "sku": "PROBE-ORD-{{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "Order probe item",
  "brand": "TestBrand",
  "image": "https://cdn.devtunde.com/item.png",
  "categoryPublicId": "{{category.response.body.publicId}}",
  "mrp": 15000.00,
  "sellingPrice": 12000.00
}

### 10 — Setup: stock the shelf (10 units)
# @name stock
# Expected: 201 — an OPENING movement is recorded
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
  "quantity": 10,
  "lowStockThreshold": 1
}

### 11 — THE HAPPY PATH: cash checkout, 2 units
# @name order
# Expected: 201 — status PAID, totalKobo 2400000, displayTotal ₦24000.00,
# line snapshot unitPriceKobo 1200000, customerPublicId absent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 12 — Card checkout with a terminal reference — the reference echoes back
# Expected: 201 — paymentMethod CARD, paymentReference "TERM-PROBE-1"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentReference": "TERM-PROBE-1"
}

### 13 — Insufficient stock: ask for 100, the shelf holds 7 (10 - 2 - 1)
# Expected: 409 — shortfalls[0].requested 100, shortfalls[0].available 7,
# stock UNCHANGED (nothing committed, no holds — Q6)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 100
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 14 — A product this store has never listed
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 15 — Quantity zero
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 0
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 16 — Quantity above 999
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1000
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 17 — An empty basket
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 18 — Missing payment method
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

### 19 — A payment method outside CASH/CARD/TRANSFER
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CHEQUE"
}

### 20 — A well-formed phone nobody has enrolled — never a silent walk-in
# Expected: 400 — "No customer with phone ... Enroll them first."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH",
  "customerPhone": "+2348099990002"
}

### 21 — Setup: the seat admin enrolls a customer under the canonical phone
# @name enroll
# Expected: 201 (200 on a later re-run — idempotent enroll)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Loyal Shopper",
  "phone": "+2348093030304"
}

### 22 — The till types the LOCAL format — normalized at the boundary (Q8)
# Expected: 201 — customerPublicId = the enrolled customer's publicId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH",
  "customerPhone": "08093030304"
}

### 23 — Setup: hire a SALES_ATTENDANT (the title-gate persona)
# @name hireAttendant
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Order Attendant",
  "email": "ord-attendant-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234569",
  "jobTitle": "SALES_ATTENDANT"
}

### 24 — Setup: the attendant logs in
# @name attendantLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hireAttendant.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 25 — The attendant checks out — the title gate refuses (Q1)
# Expected: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{attendantLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 26 — Setup: hire a SECOND cashier who will never open a session
# @name hireSessionless
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Order Sessionless Cashier",
  "email": "ord-sessionless-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234570",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 27 — Setup: the sessionless cashier logs in
# @name sessionlessLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hireSessionless.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 28 — A valid cashier with NO session checks out — the session gate fires
# Expected: 409 — "Open a session first." (precondition beats validation:
# the basket here is even garbage, and the 409 still wins)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{sessionlessLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 29 — Anonymous checkout — no token at all
# Expected: 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}
